"""
llm_factory.py — UPDATED (routes through model_router for auto-fallback)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT CHANGED FROM PREVIOUS VERSION:
1. Calls model_router.resolve() to check if active model should switch
2. Calls model_router.record_usage() after chain runs (via token tracker hook)
3. Adds deepseek provider branch
4. NEW: Supports external student server configs via _external flag

NOTHING BREAKS:
- get_llm_for_agent() same signature
- All 8 agents call it the same way
- set_runtime_key() same signature
- Gemini function_calling fix is still in the agent files
- If model_router import fails, falls back to original direct behavior

HOW AUTO-SWITCHING WORKS:
Agent calls get_llm_for_agent("location", temperature=0.3)
  -> factory gets active model (e.g. gemini-flash)
  -> calls model_router.resolve("gemini-flash", "location")
  -> router checks: has gemini-flash exceeded token threshold?
  -> if YES: returns "groq-llama" instead
  -> factory builds ChatGroq instead of ChatGoogleGenerativeAI
  -> agent never knows. tracked_chain never knows. orchestrator never knows.

HOW EXTERNAL CONFIGS WORK:
When selected_config points to a student server config:
  -> api.py registers it in router_manager._configs with _external=True
  -> api.py sets _active_external_config thread-local
  -> get_llm_for_agent() detects this and builds a ChatOpenAI pointing
     to our /external/chat/{config_name} proxy endpoint
  -> proxy forwards to student server
  -> agent never knows the difference
"""

